    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Cat 2 Test Runner — Calendar Scheduling\n\n**What it does:** For each test case in the Calendar Scheduling Tests sheet (Test Input tab), it:\n1. Snapshots the Google Calendar BEFORE (event IDs)\n2. Calls the Telegram VA - Command Handler workflow with a [TEST_MODE] prefix → the AI Agent runs and schedules an event\n3. Waits for sync, then snapshots AFTER\n4. Diffs the snapshots to find the new event the AI created\n5. Logs to the category2_results tab (test_id, proposed_day/start/end, event_id, ai_output, response_time_ms)\n6. Deletes the just-created event so the next test starts clean\n7. Waits, then moves to the next test\n\n**Configurable:**\n- How many tests to run per execution\n- Google Calendar credential on the calendar nodes\n\n**Output:** One row per test in the category2_results tab. Then run the Apps Script grading step to compute Strict_Pass + Lenient_Pass.\n\n**Required pre-setup:**\n1. A tab called category2_results in the Calendar Scheduling Tests spreadsheet with header row:\n   timestamp | test_id | ai_output | new_event_count | event_id | event_title | proposed_day | proposed_start_iso | proposed_end_iso | response_time_ms\n2. A Google Calendar credential attached to: Snapshot BEFORE, Snapshot AFTER, Delete Event\n3. The Telegram VA - Command Handler workflow's AI Agent prompt includes the TEST_MODE clause",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 880
      },
